// Title: Delete Important Scheduled Task
// ID: dbc1f800-0fe0-4bc0-9c66-292c2abe3f78
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-09
// Tags: attack.impact, attack.t1489
// Description: Detects when adversaries stop services or processes by deleting their respective scheduled tasks in order to conduct data destructive activities
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_/delete*" or process.command_line like "*_-delete*")) and ((process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\BitLocker*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\ExploitGuard*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\SystemRestore\\SR*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\UpdateOrchestrator\\*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\Windows Defender\\*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\WindowsBackup\\*" or process.command_line like "*_\\Windows\\WindowsUpdate\\*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\schtasks.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "schtasks.exe")))
